From: kadie@cs.uiuc.edu (Carl M Kadie)
Subject: A (positive) example of student archives
Message-ID: <CJG8vF.Hy3@cs.uiuc.edu>
Date: Tue, 11 Jan 1994 05:06:51 GMT

Students in the College of Engineering at the U. of Illinois
(Urbana-Champaign) can set up their own WWW pages. The references is
    http://www.cen.uiuc.edu/

It looks like references to http://www.cen.uiuc.edu/~USERID/ are
mapped to the ~USERID/public_html/

This scheme seems to have several things going for it:

   As engineering students we pay an explict fee for the engineering
   workstations. (A fee above and beyond the general university
   computer fee.) This makes it is harder to accuse us of misusing the
   state's charity.

   It looks like the space for each user's WWW pages comes out of his
   or her home directory (under a diskspace quota).

   There is no "official" index. So if you find something that offends
   you, you can't (shouldn't) blame the U.

The only risk I see in the scheme is if someone's pages becomes so
popular that access slows the server or the local net.

Have other schools done this? How is it working?

- Carl

