Carl M. Kadie (kadie@eff.org) wrote:
: CYBERSPACE-SHIP ENTERPRISE. Though commercial uses of the Internet have
: been growing rapidly, Educom VP Mike Roberts says that "for every greedy
: guy who shows up on the network trying to make a buck, there will be people
: around with something of equal value that's available for free. That will
: be do a lot to thwart the greed." (New York Times Week in Review 1/2/94 p.
: 5)  

To many people, paying a little bit of money to get a better source of
information is a bargain.  And what appears to be "greed" to many is
simply a professional's rational pricing of his services in the 
marketplace.  Right now "free" newsgroups don't appear to be the be-all 
and end-all of the information age.  We really need, I believe, to go to 
more emphasis on the "editorial" side of things where editorial services 
are valued appropriately and diversity of information sources is 
maintained at high quality via unbridled, commercial, editorial competition.
